{"id":"20260825T180821.688448198Z-00191306","time":"2026-08-25T18:08:21.688448198Z","session_id":"session-20260825T180614.482207031Z","task_id":"task-1787681174482432419","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  The transcript in internal/tui cannot be scrolled: once the conversation is longer than the window, earlier lines run off the top and there is no way to reach them.\n\nMake the transcript scrollable through the ordinary bubbletea surface. A transcript longer than the window must show its most recent lines and tell the reader that earlier ones exist; PgUp must reveal previously hidden lines; PgDn must return towards the newest; scrolling past the start must rest at the first line rather than running off it or emptying the screen; and a transcript that fits must claim nothing is hidden. How the window is tracked is yours to decide.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Model stores transcript entries in lines, handles Bubble Tea key presses in Update, and currently makes overflow inaccessible by retaining only the final available wrapped rows in View. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The existing layout test covers wrapped-row padding but does not cover transcript windowing or navigation. (internal/tui/layout_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei's scoped briefing identifies Model, Model.Update, Model.View, and Model.scroll as the relevant model symbols for this task. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei directly governs model.go with the active critical invariant that provider authentication credentials remain owned by the native provider client. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei reports no direct invariant, forbidden fix, or required test for layout_test.go. (internal/tui/layout_test.go) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: human-authority-required\n"}
